The Ogilvy Group is looking for the next generation of thought leaders, innovators, and curious minds. Those who dare to play, who never stop learning and value ideas over egos. Your own curiosity has gotten you this far; now see if it can earn you a spot at The Ogilvy Group.  &nbsp;

  Please note: The application deadline is January 19 , 2027, at 11:59 p.m. ET. &nbsp;

The Summer Internship Program: &nbsp;

Ready to gain hands-on experience working with live client briefs and contribute to work that makes a cultural impact? Our Summer Internship is the place for you. For 10 weeks between June and August, experience all that the advertising industry has to offer - from hands-on, immersive experiences and mentorship to access to tools and development opportunities.&nbsp; &nbsp;

Our Summer Internship offers placements across a variety of departments within The Ogilvy Group, including Ogilvy, Ogilvy Health, Grey and Village Marketing. Examples of these roles and areas include:&nbsp;

• Account Management &nbsp;

• Brand Planning Strategy &nbsp;

• Consulting &nbsp;

• Influencer Strategy &nbsp;

• New Business &nbsp;

• Project Management &amp; Operations &nbsp;

• Public Relations &nbsp;

• Social Strategy &nbsp;

Please note:  The application for internships within the creative craft ( i.e. art direction , copywriting , content creation, design , and production ) is separate from this one and can be found on our careers page.

The Fine Print: &nbsp;

• Locations: The 202 7 Summer Internship Program will be offered in our Chicago and New York offices. &nbsp;

• Hybrid Model: This is a full-time (35-40 hours a week) paid internship that operates in a hybrid model, with 3-4 days expected to be in office. To ensure you can fully immerse yourself in our collaborative culture, come the start of the program in June, you must be located within a commutable distance of the office you plan to work in.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Eligibility: All applicants must be current undergraduate juniors and have current and future U.S. work authorization. &nbsp;

